from pathlib import Path
from html import escape as e
import json
root=Path(__file__).parent
r=json.loads((root/'requirements.json').read_text())['items']
screens=[('Homepage','index.html','Three audience cards, optional tools, registration drawers, explainer module and general enquiries.'),('For clients','for-clients/','Team models, roles, practice areas, project-value benchmark calculator, full registration and FAQs.'),('For consultants','for-consultants/','Three role registration variants, assessment journey, earnings-potential calculator, role-specific registration and FAQs.'),('For consulting firms','for-consulting-firms/','Challenges, partnership journey, partnership-potential calculator, full registration and FAQs.')]
cards=''.join(f'<a class="review-card" href="{url}?v=why-overview-1"><h2>{title} ↗</h2><p>{desc}</p><span class="review-status">{"Needs clarification · choices" if title=="For consultants" else "Approved · updates for review"}</span></a>' for title,url,desc in screens)
rows=''.join(f'<tr><td>{x["id"]}</td><td><strong>{e(x["item"])}</strong><br>{e(x["question"])}</td><td>{e(x["status"])}</td><td>{e(x["owner"])}</td></tr>' for x in r)
html=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"><title>Public website review | OptimIQ Consultus</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="site.css?v=why-overview-1"></head><body><main class="review-main"><a class="text-link" href="../index.html?v=why-overview-1#public-website-review">← All client review screens</a><p class="eyebrow">PUBLIC WEBSITE · APPROVED DESIGN 1</p><h1>Design 1 approved with changes.</h1><p>The homepage and audience journeys use the same visual system. Feedback 2 restores the existing registration fields and keeps desktop navigation visible on mobile. Why OptimIQ now summarises the complete offering: certified capability, local–global teams, scoping and delivery support, flexible terms, consultant opportunities and firm growth. Client approval recorded on 1 November 2026. Feedback 1 is implemented for review: all three audience calculator models, their inputs, ranges and related wording follow the client reference. The three branded concept-note PDFs and email-only download simulator are also ready. Email is not saved; backend storage will be connected later. Further feedback will be provided one by one. The preview sends no enquiries, applications or messages.</p><div class="review-grid">{cards}</div><section class="review-section"><h2>What is ready for review</h2><p>Shared navigation, full registration forms, deep links, calculator confirmation, optional attachments and concept-note email/download dialogs, role selection, mobile actions, FAQs, video fallbacks and form validation. Registration now matches the existing source forms, including the three consultant role variants, grouped options and file fields. The original empty option lists are marked Needs clarification.</p><p><a href="REVIEW-TESTS.md">Verification results</a> · <a href="README.md">Developer handover</a></p></section><section class="review-section"><h2>Client assets and decisions still needed</h2><p>These items are tracked separately from screen readiness. No missing asset or proposed business assumption is treated as approved. The member portal and existing staging registration pages have not been changed.</p><table class="review-table"><thead><tr><th>Reference</th><th>Required input or decision</th><th>Status</th><th>Owner to nominate</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows}</tbody></table></section><section class="review-section"><h2>Review assumptions</h2><p>The public role label remains Consultant, matching the approved portal. The designer’s Strategy Consultant label needs confirmation. The nine practice labels are proposed public wording and require mapping to the authoritative business master. All three client concept notes are supplied and branded; email capture is simulated until the backend is connected. Legacy registration details and source gaps are recorded in feedback-02.md. The required films remain visible as review placeholders with readable overviews.</p><p>Public forms currently validate and prepare a local preview only. Production success states require durable backend receipt; verification wording appears only after an actual queued-email response. Mocked service tests do not count as a live integration test.</p></section></main></body></html>'''
(root/'review.html').write_text(html,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built public website review inventory and dependency register.')
